---
import '@fontsource-variable/roboto-serif';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const TURNSTILE_SITEKEY = '0x4AAAAAAEcCwzuExy2fSCmH';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Embedded Product Builder or Agency? | Saielle DaSilva"
  description="How to choose between hiring an agency and embedding one senior product builder in your team, including the cases where the agency is the right answer."
>
  <section class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Build &amp; delivery</p>
      <h1>One builder inside your team, or an agency around it.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        For teams deciding how to get something built when they cannot build it themselves.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        You have a thing that needs building and no capacity to build it. Two
        obvious routes: a firm, which brings a team and a process, or one
        senior person who sits inside yours. They are different purchases, and
        the sales material on both sides blurs that.
      </p>

      <h2>When an agency is the right answer</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>The scope is known and the work is mostly volume.</li>
        <li>You need several disciplines at once and do not have any of them.</li>
        <li>What you want at the end is production software with a warranty.</li>
        <li>The work has to continue whether or not one person is available.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        In all four cases a firm will serve you better than I will, and I will
        say so on the call rather than after the invoice.
      </p>

      <h2>When one embedded builder is the right answer</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Nobody can yet write the brief an agency would need.</li>
        <li>The question is whether the idea works, not how to scale it.</li>
        <li>You want your own team to end up understanding the thing.</li>
        <li>The environment is the hard part: your data, your systems, your constraints.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        An agency will build what the brief says. That is a strength when the
        brief is right and an expensive problem when it is not. The reason to
        embed one person is to find out what the brief should have said, while
        building it.
      </p>

      <h2>What is different in practice</h2>
      <p>
        A firm brings its own environment, its own process and a team that
        changes. Work happens over there and arrives here. An embedded builder
        works in your environment from the first week. That is slower to start
        and it tells you far more, because everything you would have hit during
        integration turns up in week one instead.
      </p>
      <p>
        The trade is real and it runs both ways. One person is one person. No
        bench, no cover, and a hard limit on how much gets built. If that
        limit is the problem, you want the firm.
      </p>

      <h2>What it costs, both ways</h2>
      <p>
        I charge a day rate and publish it, so the arithmetic is yours to do:
        the shape and the numbers are on the
        {' '}<a href="/forward-deployed/">forward deployed product building</a>
        {' '}page. Agencies generally quote by project, which buys you
        certainty on price and costs you flexibility on scope. Neither is
        cheaper in the abstract. The cheaper one is whichever matches how well
        you can describe what you want.
      </p>

      <h2>A third answer</h2>
      <p>
        Sometimes the honest answer is neither. If the problem is that nobody
        senior owns product direction, buying build capacity produces a
        well-built version of an unresolved argument. That is
        {' '}<a href="/fractional/">fractional and interim leadership</a>, and
        it is usually cheaper than finding out the other way.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="contact-form-section" aria-label="Get in touch">
      <div class="contact-card">
        <h2>Let's talk.</h2>
        <p class="form-lede">
          If you are weighing this up and want a straight answer about which one you need, ask me.
        </p>
        <form id="contact-form" novalidate>
          <input type="hidden" name="source" value="embedded-or-agency" />
          <div class="form-grid">
            <label>
              <span class="form-label">Name</span>
              <input type="text" name="name" required autocomplete="name" />
            </label>
            <label>
              <span class="form-label">Email</span>
              <input type="email" name="email" required autocomplete="email" />
            </label>
          </div>
          <label>
            <span class="form-label">What's this about?</span>
            <select name="topic">
              <option value="forward-deployed" selected>Forward deployed product building</option>
              <option value="advisor-intro">Advisor or recruiter introduction</option>
              <option value="strategic-direction">Strategic direction</option>
              <option value="execution">Execution &amp; transformation</option>
              <option value="fractional">Fractional leadership</option>
              <option value="speaking">Speaking &amp; workshops</option>
              <option value="mentoring">Mentoring</option>
              <option value="other">Something else</option>
            </select>
          </label>
          <label>
            <span class="form-label">Message</span>
            <textarea name="message" rows="5" required></textarea>
          </label>
          {
            TURNSTILE_SITEKEY && (
              <>
                <div
                  class="cf-turnstile"
                  data-sitekey={TURNSTILE_SITEKEY}
                  data-theme="light"
                />
                <script
                  is:inline
                  src="https://challenges.cloudflare.com/turnstile/v0/api.js"
                  async
                  defer
                />
              </>
            )
          }
          <button class="btn-plain" type="submit">Send it</button>
          <p class="form-status" id="form-status" role="status"></p>
        </form>
      </div>
      <p class="faq-link">
        Questions first? <a href="/faq/">Read the FAQ.</a>
      </p>
    </section>
  </section>

  <script>
    const ENDPOINT = 'https://contact-form.intentionaut.workers.dev/contact';
    const form = document.getElementById('contact-form');

    form?.addEventListener('submit', async (e) => {
      e.preventDefault();
      const data = Object.fromEntries(new FormData(form));
      const statusEl = document.getElementById('form-status');

      try {
        const res = await fetch(ENDPOINT, {
          method: 'POST',
          headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
          body: JSON.stringify(data),
        });
        const result = await res.json();
        if (res.ok) {
          form.reset();
          if (statusEl) statusEl.textContent = result.message || "Thank you; I'll reply soon.";
        } else {
          if (statusEl) statusEl.textContent = result.error || 'Something went wrong; please email me directly.';
        }
      } catch {
        if (statusEl) statusEl.textContent = 'Something went wrong; please email me directly.';
      }
    });
  </script>
</BaseLayout>
